  "notes": [
    "Fourteenth single-TU promotion on this line: a dActor_c subclass whose TU owns its own key function and therefore emits its vtable and RTTI.",
    "The class was coined VolcanoFire until the rename immediately before this promotion. The cartridge spells it at ov022:0x02114434/0x02114440, and promotion needs that name: the compiler's _ZTS bytes have to equal the cartridge's, which no coined spelling can achieve.",
    "daObj_volcanoCannon_c_classInit's vptr store is (int)&_ZTV21daObj_volcanoCannon_c[2], not the bare symbol. Once the TU emits the vtable, mwcc's symbol is the storage start at 0x02114474 and the ROM stores the address point eight bytes later. Every byte gate is blind to this -- a relocated word is a wildcard -- and objisolate's addend check is what catches it.",
    "The destructor is defined inline in include/daObj_volcanoCannon_c.h and declared first in the class body. Out of line, mwccarm emits D2/D0/D1 while the cartridge holds D1 (0x021125e0) then D0 (0x02112610) and no D2 at all, and objisolate refuses the object for emitting out of ROM address order.",
    "func_ov022_02112654, func_ov022_021126ac and func_ov022_02112710 are this class's state callbacks, kept as ROM-named external functions rather than made file-local: the State record the module sinit builds at ov022:0x02114690 names their addresses, and that sinit is not part of this TU.",
    "The two eight-byte records at 0x02114424 and 0x0211442c are the pointer-to-member constants that sinit copies into that State record. They are deliberately left OUTSIDE this TU's .data claim: this TU declares no static State object, so mwccarm emits no such constants, and claiming bytes nothing in the TU produces would fail the run.",
    "daObj_volcanoCannon_c_classInit and g_profile_OBJ_VOLCANO_CANNON are reconstructed source-style names: SM64DS proves the RTTI class, the OBJ_VOLCANO_CANNON registry ID, the descriptor/factory relationship, the 0x11c allocation and the vtable identity; later EAD lineage supplies the spelling prior. Historical aliases were VolcanoFire_Spawn and VolcanoFire_SpawnInfo."
  ],
